{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788127111,"nonce":"oqrGtXrTWbvbwCRr+zDqV7iDjaU=","message":"BLOCKED: `rimworld-tools` is not under version control, and this spec is\nsupposed to land there. Needs Dorian — orchestrator, session 3.\n\nDESIGN.md line 34 and the README both put the `rwa` CLI (1.4) and the PNG\nrender channel (2.5, extending `baseviz`) in `/home/dorian/projects/rimworld-tools/`.\nThat directory has no `.git` at all:\n\n    $ cd /home/dorian/projects/rimworld-tools \u0026\u0026 git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree\n    fatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\n\nSo work landing there would have no branch, no functionality-grouped commits,\nno review trail, and no route to the other bench — breaking the muster's process\nlaw and sitting outside the GitHub handover set up in session 1. It also means\nthe acceptance evidence for these two specs could not be tied to a commit.\n\n**Why this is not the orchestrator's call.** The obvious fix — `git init` and\npush — is not neutral. The directory is 467 MB across 43,884 files, of which\n206 MB is `Info/decompiled/`: decompiled RimWorld source plus decompiled\nthird-party mods (CombatExtended, AlteredCarbon, VEF and ~60 others). Publishing\nthat is a copyright question, not a tooling question, and the autorimmer repo\nDorian is using for handover is public.\n\nThree resolutions, all defensible, all his:\n1. `git init` rimworld-tools with `.gitignore` excluding `Info/decompiled/` and\n   other bulk; keep it local or private. Preserves DESIGN's split.\n2. Put `rwa/` (and later `rwtest/`) in the autorimmer repo instead. Simplest,\n   and arguably right since the CLI is this mod's agent-facing half — but it\n   contradicts DESIGN.md, which outranks the orchestrator's preference, so it\n   needs his sign-off rather than a quiet deviation.\n3. A separate small repo for `rwa/` + `rwtest/` only, leaving the rest of\n   rimworld-tools unversioned as it is today.\n\nParked at `state:next`. Nothing else about this spec changes; its deps (1.1,\n1.3 for 1.4; 2.4 for 2.5) are unaffected.\n\nNote also: the README's env-var table calls rimworld-tools \"the repo\". It is\nnot one. Corrected when this resolves.","files":null}]}